    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d793">

                <pb facs="0958" n="942" sameAs="frus:frus1947v08/pg942"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711F.1914/12–1147: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Panama</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hines</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">urgent</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">niact</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Panamá</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1947-12-11T10:00:00-05:00">December 11,
                            1947—10 a.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>723. Accompanied by General Hale,<anchor n="69" xml:id="d793-f1"/> I called on
                    President this morning to thank him for cooperation shown in signing agreement.
                    He is extremely anxious that reply to note transmitted in Embtel 710, December 6<anchor n="70"
                        xml:id="d793-f2"/> be received by time Assembly convenes tomorrow since he
                    feels certain that, if couched in favorable terms, it would make certain
                    ratification by that body.</p>
                <p>Confirming today’s conversation with Newbegin I most strongly urge I be
                    authorized immediately to reaffirm in writing the verbal assurances previously
                    given Panama. Even if we only state that Department will make appropriate
                    recommendations to Congress, such assurance if made at this time would have
                    powerful effect on Assembly and on critical political situation now brewing.</p>
                <p>The opposition is presently organizing behind Alfaro who recently told Jimenez
                    that, if he did not get promise from US of economic assistance before signing
                    agreement, he could whistle for it after. This is the impression we must combat
                    at once.</p>
                <p>Furthermore, I believe that our promise to return Paitilla and other parcels to
                    Panama, which involves no drawn-out negotiations, should be presented as a
                    “must” to the present Congress if we are not to be exposed to accusations of bad
                    faith.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hines</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
